This repository holds the source code of the Ozimut website. It is published so that
anyone can read it, study how the site works and check what it does with data.
It is NOT open-source software: publishing the code grants no right to reuse it.

1. What you may do

   - Read the code, here or in a copy you download or clone for that purpose.
   - Fork the repository on GitHub, within what GitHub's Terms of Service give every
     user (viewing and forking on GitHub itself).
   - Quote short excerpts to discuss, review or cite the project, naming their source.

2. What needs the copyright holder's prior written permission

   - Copying, modifying, merging, publishing, distributing, sublicensing or selling
     the code, the texts or the pictures, or any substantial part of them.
   - Running the code, or a work derived from it, as a website, a service or an
     application — for yourself or for others, whether or not for money.
   - Using the code, the texts or the data to train, tune or evaluate
     machine-learning models.

   To ask: contact@ozimut.com.

